================================================================================
SERVICES REACHED AT RUN TIME
================================================================================

OGS                 online-go.com. Go reads your public record there by the user name you
                    type: your rating and its deviation, and your games. The user name is the
                    one thing sent, and no login is used.
The Go relay        127.0.0.1:8766, on your own computer (scripts/go-relay.mjs). Go sends the
                    positions of your games through it to KataGo, which runs on the same
                    computer; nothing leaves it.
The C++ runner      127.0.0.1:8767, on your own computer (scripts/cpp-runner.mjs). The C++
                    course sends the programs you write, with each test's input, to it; it
                    compiles them with GCC on the same computer and sends back what they print.
                    Nothing leaves the computer.
AtCoder             atcoder.jp. The C++ course links to the contests and to your public
                    contest record there; you paste the record into Eruko. Eruko itself
                    sends AtCoder nothing.

SQLite (public domain) is served from this app (src/record/sqlite-3.54.0/, as sqlite.org ships
it), not from a CDN. It keeps your record in this browser.

